WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.487 --> 00:00:07.934
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.739
Hm, if I was hardcore,

00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:27.953
I'd be able to roll my Rs
when I sang the song.

00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:29.498
Generaaall...

00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:30.467
Gen'rrrrrll...

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:31.705
Generrrlll...

00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:32.881
Gen[chokes]

00:00:32.881 --> 00:00:34.033
...I-I can't do it.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.529
I guess that's why
I'm not a REAL general.

00:00:36.529 --> 00:00:38.598
They can probably all sing properly.

00:00:38.598 --> 00:00:41.567
So, back to the trenches for me.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.567
Literally.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.677
I guess this really is
my new job now: killing people.

00:00:46.677 --> 00:00:47.834
I've had worse.

00:00:48.355 --> 00:00:49.920
Good.  No tanks.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.443
Cleaning out grease traps--

00:00:51.443 --> 00:00:52.834
Whoa!  What is--

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.442
YEAH! HOW DO YOU LIKE EARTH'S GRAVITY?!

00:00:55.442 --> 00:00:56.767
NICE PARACHUTE!

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.304
HEY, A PLANE! OVER HERE!

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:00.962
The plane ignored me.

00:01:00.962 --> 00:01:04.688
Maybe the Air Force isn't in on
the same conspiracy to kill me.

00:01:04.688 --> 00:01:05.936
Well, I shot at it.

00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:08.962
That's what you're supposed to
do to signal rescue choppers, right?

00:01:08.962 --> 00:01:11.000
Or maybe that's just in the south.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.287
I know that's how they do it
in Florida and Louisiana.

00:01:14.287 --> 00:01:17.345
So, another minefield.

00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:19.250
Is this sign bluffing?

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.673
Prooooobably not!

00:01:21.673 --> 00:01:25.688
When the hell did they have time
to plant a minefield around here anyway?

00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:27.825
It must've been a rush job.

00:01:27.825 --> 00:01:29.734
They probably didn't even make a map.

00:01:30.129 --> 00:01:30.667
[lock jiggles]

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.467
Oh.  Yeah.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:33.589
[lock jiggles]

00:01:33.589 --> 00:01:34.334
Yeah.

00:01:35.023 --> 00:01:37.500
I'll bet anything those mines
aren't documented.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.127
That means in 20 years, some
documentary maker's going to come here

00:01:43.127 --> 00:01:46.149
and get his legs blown off
trying to film this place.

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:48.452
Here's to you, future dude.

00:01:48.452 --> 00:01:49.701
Oh! There's--

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.586
[wall crumbling]
JESUS CHRIST!

00:01:51.586 --> 00:01:54.190
THAT DEBRIS COULD'VE
TRIGGERED THE TRIPMINE!

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.111
CLEARLY WE DIDN'T HAVE ENOUGH
REGULAR MINES FOR THIS SIDE,

00:01:57.111 --> 00:02:00.100
SO WE ADDED SOME EXPOSED ONES
NEXT TO FALLING RUBBLE!

00:02:00.699 --> 00:02:04.267
BECAUSE WE HAVEN'T BOMBED THIS PLACE
ENOUGH ALREADY, IS THAT THE IDEA?!

00:02:04.618 --> 00:02:05.550
[wall crumbling]

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.901
OH MY GOD!

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:11.185
IS THERE A SQUIRREL UP THERE ON
THE ROOF OR SOMETHING?!

00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:13.133
This could be payback...?!

00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:17.832
I don't see anything.

00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:20.414
I don't understand why
we have all these tripmines.

00:02:20.414 --> 00:02:23.167
I guess the idea is if
an alien comes by here...

00:02:24.221 --> 00:02:26.520
...we blow it up and
the side of a building.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.033
Oh, this one's sneaky;
trying to trip me.

00:02:31.229 --> 00:02:32.306
[wall crumbling]
What?

00:02:32.306 --> 00:02:34.011
OH GOD, NO! NOT NOW!

00:02:34.011 --> 00:02:35.903
WuuaaaAAAAA-AAA-AAA!

00:02:35.903 --> 00:02:36.838
[exhales]

00:02:36.838 --> 00:02:39.500
This must be how
old people feel about stairs...

00:02:40.028 --> 00:02:42.511
Oh, another dead guy.

00:02:42.511 --> 00:02:43.601
That's nice...

00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:48.525
Well, he didn't die from a mine;
he still has all his body parts attached.

00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:49.067
Maybe--

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:49.389
[gunshot]

00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:53.009
WAAAAHHH!  WAAAHHH!
WAAAAH-WOOH-WEEHH-WAAA!
WAAH...!

00:02:53.009 --> 00:02:53.767
[exhales]

00:02:54.421 --> 00:02:54.856
[gunshot]

00:02:54.856 --> 00:02:57.846
Oh my GOD, that was close!

00:02:57.846 --> 00:03:00.904
Wait, is this that same sniper
from last night?

00:03:00.904 --> 00:03:02.367
Is he following me?!

00:03:02.824 --> 00:03:04.286
I knew it!

00:03:04.286 --> 00:03:06.523
That guy is fucking evil!

00:03:06.523 --> 00:03:10.482
He shot at me and practically
herded me into this tripmine here.

00:03:10.482 --> 00:03:11.300
Vicious...

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:16.000
Hello!

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:18.367
RRRAAAAAAAGHHHHH!

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.817
Why is this door to nowhere locked?!

00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:22.601
Are they afraid people were
going to drive through here

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.249
and park on the minefield?

00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:26.432
I guess that is a valid concern!

00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:30.194
Well, I'm not walking through the
God-damned minefield so I've got a problem!

00:03:30.194 --> 00:03:33.900
I'm not going to climb this ramp;
sniper'll pick me off for sure!

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.138
And this suit is still
blaze-fucking-orange!

00:03:37.138 --> 00:03:40.676
I haven't been shot enough times
to wear all the paint off yet!

00:03:40.676 --> 00:03:42.354
Looks like this door is my best chance,

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:45.444
even though I have no reason to
think it's unlocked.

00:03:45.444 --> 00:03:48.262
I guess I'll just...
wing it if it doesn't work.

00:03:48.262 --> 00:03:50.801
Whoa-whoa-whoa.  Wake up!

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.263
Yeah, that's kind of
where my life is right now,

00:03:53.263 --> 00:03:56.361
where I know my best option
isn't going to work.

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:58.667
Okay, so let's go and NOT do this!

00:03:59.245 --> 00:04:00.145
Yep, it's fucking locked.

00:04:00.145 --> 00:04:03.097
Zig-zag, zig-zag, zig-zag,
zig-zig-zag-zagzagzigizz...

00:04:03.097 --> 00:04:05.205
Hah...that could've gone worse.

00:04:05.205 --> 00:04:09.510
Any day where you don't have your brains
painted against the wall isn't all bad.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.453
Well, YOU know what I'm talking about.

00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:14.634
Okay, surely a sniper
can't hit a moving target...

00:04:16.061 --> 00:04:16.701
Good...

00:04:18.741 --> 00:04:20.746
Yeah, I better stay out of there.

00:04:20.746 --> 00:04:23.181
I didn't realize this
was a sniper preserve.

00:04:23.181 --> 00:04:25.164
That must be what all the
landmines are for:

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.934
to keep them from wandering
into the residential areas.

00:04:28.697 --> 00:04:31.285
It's for their own protection
just as much as ours.

00:04:31.285 --> 00:04:32.482
If we let them run free,

00:04:32.482 --> 00:04:35.538
then they'd snipe everything in
sight and run out of the bullets.

00:04:35.538 --> 00:04:37.500
It would disrupt the ecosystem.

00:04:38.748 --> 00:04:40.854
[distant gunshots]

00:04:40.854 --> 00:04:42.801
Yep, see, I hear them.

00:04:43.447 --> 00:04:44.399
[electrical arcing]

00:04:44.399 --> 00:04:49.114
Oh, wow.  Looks like I made the right call
not tiptoeing through the minefield.

00:04:49.114 --> 00:04:51.672
I don't think I could jump
to that fence from here.

00:04:51.672 --> 00:04:55.510
And, if they were smart--which is
a big "if"--but, if they were,

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.778
it would put the mines right at
the fence where I would land.

00:04:58.778 --> 00:04:59.870
That's what I would do.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.068
Okay, so what's the plan now?
Besides more sunburn?

00:05:04.068 --> 00:05:05.387
Ah, that'll work.

00:05:05.387 --> 00:05:07.605
I don't even have to be
Jackie Chan to do this one,

00:05:07.605 --> 00:05:09.601
which is good for...obvious reasons.

00:05:12.047 --> 00:05:14.765
Okay, so the aliens don't come
from a swamp planet,

00:05:14.765 --> 00:05:17.334
but their gravity has to be
lower than ours.

00:05:18.098 --> 00:05:19.874
That flier dropped off aliens

00:05:19.874 --> 00:05:23.609
while it was two stories in the
air--just fucking free-falling.

00:05:23.609 --> 00:05:25.767
Apparently, they saw no problem with that.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:29.425
That's considered normal and
perfectly safe where they come from.

00:05:29.425 --> 00:05:30.940
Holy crap!

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.812
So, if I had made it passed the minefield,

00:05:32.812 --> 00:05:36.591
then I would've had to climb through
barbed wire so I could be electrocuted.

00:05:36.591 --> 00:05:38.719
Jesus, I don't think they
have to worry about

00:05:38.719 --> 00:05:41.567
coyotes digging through the
trash around here.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.827
And I'm sure that door is to a
room filled with candy and treasure,

00:05:46.827 --> 00:05:48.829
but getting there is just not happening.

00:05:48.829 --> 00:05:53.122
I bet the soldiers would put landmines on
the roof if they could.  Just to be sure.

00:05:53.122 --> 00:05:55.367
All right, this looks like my entrance.

00:05:57.255 --> 00:05:59.571
...if I had an acetylene torch...

00:05:59.571 --> 00:06:02.523
I still can't get over the
aliens jumping from that height.

00:06:02.523 --> 00:06:05.106
Are the aliens bad at math?

00:06:05.106 --> 00:06:08.652
I guess it's possible; they only have
three fingers and we have five.

00:06:08.652 --> 00:06:11.903
Nobody believes me, but I think
we'd be farther along technologically

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:13.775
if we had six fingers on each hand.

00:06:13.775 --> 00:06:16.960
I mean, for God's sake, the gene
for polydactyly is dominant.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.200
I have no doubt that--
WHOA, what am I doing?

00:06:19.864 --> 00:06:22.500
Not getting shot,
I think that's what I'm doing.

00:06:24.916 --> 00:06:28.713
Yeah, there's people that give you
the evil eye, and then there's snipers.

00:06:28.713 --> 00:06:30.041
Big difference.

00:06:30.041 --> 00:06:35.225
But, yeah, I feel certain working with a
duodecimal system would make us better people.

00:06:35.225 --> 00:06:38.256
I think we'd all be surprised how
many of our problems would be solved

00:06:38.256 --> 00:06:39.828
if we all had twelve fingers.

00:06:39.828 --> 00:06:41.815
Okay, this looks like my ticket.

00:06:41.815 --> 00:06:43.441
Oh! We've got a live one.

00:06:43.441 --> 00:06:44.000
Hey!

00:06:44.455 --> 00:06:47.567
Make any sudden movements and
I'm going to shoot you, okay?

00:06:48.547 --> 00:06:49.434
Okay.

00:06:50.392 --> 00:06:51.684
What's up?  Me.

00:06:51.684 --> 00:06:53.343
SCIENTIST: You're heading for
the Lambda Complex, aren't you?

00:06:53.343 --> 00:06:54.463
I have no idea.

00:06:54.463 --> 00:06:56.138
SCIENTIST: I was going there myself
until I wound up here and..

00:06:56.138 --> 00:06:57.968
well...simply lost my nerve.

00:06:58.374 --> 00:07:00.703
SCIENTIST: Take one look through
that door and you'll see what I mean.

00:07:00.703 --> 00:07:01.534
Boxes...

00:07:02.003 --> 00:07:04.557
SCIENTIST: I'm just going to wait out
the catastrophe in here!

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:08.510
SCIENTIST: If you intend to go on, then I
beg of you: proceed with extreme caution!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:11.390
Man, if it's worse than what I've seen

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.907
it must be silverback gorillas
with flamethrowers.

00:07:14.907 --> 00:07:16.320
Well, I'll be honest with you.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.365
I was thinking about shooting
you just to be safe,

00:07:19.365 --> 00:07:24.170
but I decided maybe killing scared unarmed
people doesn't make me the good guy.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:28.534
So, if you're waiting here,
do you have a deck of cards, or what?

00:07:33.079 --> 00:07:36.000
Oh, hey, how many fingers
do you have on your hands?

